d2d1: Reuse the constants already in the ring when they have not changed.

Every primitive mapped the constant buffer ring and wrote its vertex
and pixel shader constants, though consecutive primitives usually
share them: about half of Affinity's 540 draws a frame while dragging
a selection have the same constants as the draw before. Keep what was
last written and, when the new constants are the same, leave them
where they are: no map, and the bound offsets stay as they were, so
no rebinding either. A discard of the ring and Clear, which writes its
own constants there, forget it.

Affinity, three alternating rounds: dragging a selection, 3% more
frames, UI-thread time per frame -4% and wined3d's command thread
-15%; node editing, 9% more frames, -11% and -16%. The d2d1
conformance tests give the same results, and the canvas is pixel
identical.
